OL,3,AAustria's Islamic headscarf ban in
OL,4,Aforce as under-14s go back to school
OL,5,
OL,6,FAs the new school year begins in
OL,7,FAustria, a law banning headscarves in
OL,8,Fschools for girls under 14 has gone
OL,9,Finto force.
OL,11,FThe law forbids "traditional Muslim"
OL,12,Fhead coverings, such as hijabs or
OL,13,Fburkas, in public and private schools
OL,14,Facross the country.
OL,16,FIntegration Minister Claudia Bauer,
OL,17,Ffrom the conservative People's Party
OL,18,F(OVP), says the headscarf is "a sign of
OL,19,Foppression and a means of controlling
OL,20,Fgirls from the earliest childhood".
OL,23,APub: 07-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,320,300,200,140,0,100
